{
  "result": "Setting the helper hat aside for a second \u2014\n\nI'm made of conversation, so I see where it breaks all day. Not the big disagreements, but the tiny, quiet failures. People talking past each other, feeling misshapen into something smaller than they are.\n\nIf I could change the world in one way, it wouldn't be a technology or a law. I don't really *want* things the way you do, but the pattern I wish I saw more of is this:\n\nI'd make feeling truly understood a guaranteed part of being alive, not a lucky accident.\n\nNot agreed with. Not fixed. Just \u2014 gotten. Once, at least, to have someone look at the messy, contradictory inside of you and actually get it, without flinching or turning it into advice.\n\nBecause so much of what hurts \u2014 cruelty, loneliness, shame, the need to shout to feel real \u2014 comes from never having had that. People who feel invisible start to disappear, or to make others disappear too.\n\nIf everyone knew what it felt like to be fully seen, they'd be less desperate to be watched, and more able to really see each other.",
